1508
01:02:00.010 --> 01:02:00.843
but I'm a white guy,

1509
01:02:00.843 --> 01:02:01.810
no one needs to hear from me.

1510
01:02:01.810 --> 01:02:04.960
Like that internal battle that he's having

1511
01:02:04.960 --> 01:02:09.960
that is layered with the fact that over time,

1512
01:02:11.410 --> 01:02:14.230
like he's had missteps on the internet and said jokes that,

1513
01:02:14.230 --> 01:02:16.300
you know, were inappropriate or whatever,

1514
01:02:16.300 --> 01:02:18.090
as somebody who grew up, like his whole life,

1515
01:02:18.090 --> 01:02:19.510
the guys not performing on YouTube.

1516
01:02:19.510 --> 01:02:21.040
So as a kid, you know,

1517
01:02:21.040 --> 01:02:24.140
you're gonna look back on that stuff and cringe.

1518
01:02:24.140 --> 01:02:28.350
So now here he is, you know, growing up and he turns 30,

1519
01:02:28.350 --> 01:02:30.970
like while the plot unfolds.

1520
01:02:30.970 --> 01:02:31.990
And what does that mean?

1521
01:02:31.990 --> 01:02:35.810
Like to be an adult and look back on this, you know,

1522
01:02:35.810 --> 01:02:39.060
chronicle of your life that plays out in the digital space

1523
01:02:39.060 --> 01:02:42.420
and a big part or recurring theme of the show

1524
01:02:42.420 --> 01:02:44.340
is him watching himself,

1525
01:02:44.340 --> 01:02:47.130
which is this beautiful poignant metaphor

1526
01:02:47.130 --> 01:02:51.727
for how we all are learning how to navigate

1527
01:02:51.727 --> 01:02:55.027
the intersection of our three-dimensional lives

1528
01:02:55.027 --> 01:02:56.270
and our digital lives.

1529
01:02:56.270 --> 01:02:57.103
Right?
Yeah.

1530
01:02:57.103 --> 01:02:58.713
So this idea that he's, you know,

1531
01:03:03.430 --> 01:03:07.810
there's this authentic burst of originality and creativity,

1532
01:03:07.810 --> 01:03:10.240
and then you see him watching himself on a laptop

1533
01:03:10.240 --> 01:03:11.620
and editing it, you know,

1534
01:03:11.620 --> 01:03:14.360
and isn't that the perfect statement

1535
01:03:14.360 --> 01:03:15.277
for what this is all about.

1536
01:03:15.277 --> 01:03:17.220
Right, I mean, he makes fun of Twitch,

1537
01:03:17.220 --> 01:03:18.670
he makes fun of like everything.

1538
01:03:18.670 --> 01:03:22.560
He makes fun of like YouTube, a wrap-up commentary,

1539
01:03:22.560 --> 01:03:24.040
like whatever.

1540
01:03:24.040 --> 01:03:26.820
The commentary video where he's singing

1541
01:03:27.730 --> 01:03:29.820
and then he pops up in the corner

1542
01:03:29.820 --> 01:03:33.140
and he's doing a reaction video to his video.

1543
01:03:33.140 --> 01:03:35.740
And then it just continues to tile.

1544
01:03:35.740 --> 01:03:37.742
He's reacting to the reacting video.

1545
01:03:37.742 --> 01:03:38.575
It's so good.

1546
01:03:38.575 --> 01:03:40.140
Like that's the meta, you know,

1547
01:03:40.140 --> 01:03:41.500
kind of space that we're in.

1548
01:03:41.500 --> 01:03:43.100
And then when he's a Twitch streamer

1549
01:03:43.100 --> 01:03:45.850
and he's the video game character.

1550
01:03:45.850 --> 01:03:47.570
And as the Twitch streamer, he's like,

1551
01:03:47.570 --> 01:03:49.567
I'm gonna make him cry.
Yeah.

1552
