01:14:22.430 --> 01:14:26.190
Eastern philosophy that he's,

1809
01:14:26.190 --> 01:14:28.480
appropriated is the wrong word,

1810
01:14:28.480 --> 01:14:31.310
'cause he actually cared about it and studied it

1811
01:14:31.310 --> 01:14:34.053
and so I can relate to that.

1812
01:14:35.350 --> 01:14:38.554
And so, you know, definitely when he died,

1813
01:14:38.554 --> 01:14:43.554
it was shocking to be honest with you and sad.

1814
01:14:45.840 --> 01:14:48.190
But someone I always sort of admired

1815
01:14:48.190 --> 01:14:49.660
and continue to admire.

1816
01:14:49.660 --> 01:14:51.610
And I'll watch anything with him in it.

1817
01:14:51.610 --> 01:14:53.400
So I'm really looking forward to this.

1818
01:14:53.400 --> 01:14:56.080
Yeah, just utterly compelling to watch him,

1819
01:14:56.080 --> 01:14:59.240
a captivating, charismatic personality

1820
01:14:59.240 --> 01:15:04.240
who had this expansive joy for experiences of all kinds.

1821
01:15:06.700 --> 01:15:09.320
And irrespective of however successful

1822
01:15:09.320 --> 01:15:12.300
he became, was really just like one of us,

1823
01:15:12.300 --> 01:15:13.550
like he was an every man

1824
01:15:13.550 --> 01:15:16.580
and he was much more interested in having a conversation

1825
01:15:16.580 --> 01:15:17.900
with a random guy on the street

1826
01:15:17.900 --> 01:15:20.697
than he was about going to some velvet rope event.

1827
01:15:20.697 --> 01:15:23.460
And I think what's interesting about him,

1828
01:15:23.460 --> 01:15:26.050
and the documentary affirms this take

1829
01:15:26.050 --> 01:15:29.700
that I've always had, which is that this guy essentially

1830
01:15:29.700 --> 01:15:31.610
was an untreated alcoholic.

1831
01:15:31.610 --> 01:15:33.831
I mean, I'm convinced that this was the case.

1832
01:15:33.831 --> 01:15:34.664
Oh yeah, big drinker.

1833
01:15:34.664 --> 01:15:36.610
So he had this heroin problem.

1834
01:15:36.610 --> 01:15:37.823
He kicked heroin.

1835
01:15:38.860 --> 01:15:40.010
He kicked hard drugs.

1836
01:15:40.010 --> 01:15:42.759
But without going to narcotics anonymous,

1837
01:15:42.759 --> 01:15:45.770
But he's this extreme personality.

1838
01:15:45.770 --> 01:15:50.090
And that ism inside of him divorced itself

1839
01:15:50.090 --> 01:15:52.740
from hardcore substances,

1840
01:15:52.740 --> 01:15:57.080
but remained active and would latch onto anything

1841
01:15:57.080 --> 01:15:59.600
and everything that could kind of take him out

1842
01:15:59.600 --> 01:16:03.900
of whatever emotional disaffectation he was experiencing.

1843
01:16:03.900 --> 01:16:06.810
And that extremism made him this larger

1844
01:16:06.810 --> 01:16:08.393
than life personality.

1845
01:16:09.348 --> 01:16:11.500
So, it was, in many ways, his strength

1846
01:16:11.500 --> 01:16:15.260
and what endeared all of us to him so profoundly,

1847
01:16:15.260 --> 01:16:17.600
but also ultimately, you know,

1848
01:16:17.600 --> 01:16:19.700
paved the way for, for his demise.

1849
01:16:19.700 --> 01:16:21.970
I mean, he continued to drink and, you know,

1850
01:16:21.970 --> 01:16:22.900
smoke pot and stuff like that.

1851
01:16:22.900 --> 01:16:25.500
So it wasn't like he actually got sober,

1852
01:16:25.500 --> 01:16:28.620
but you see over the course of this documentary,

1853
01:16:28.620 --> 01:16:33.620
how he latches on to certain, not just substances,

1854
01:16:33.650 --> 01:16:36.480
but people, experiences.

1855
01:16:36.480 --> 01:16:39.890
Like he goes from being just the guy who's just smokes

1856
01:16:39.890 --> 01:16:43.970
like crazy to being an insane jujitsu practitioner.

1857
01:16:43.970 --> 01:16:46.120
And that becomes his obsession,

1858
01:16:46.120 --> 01:16:47.860
a healthier obsession of course,

1859
01:16:47.860 --> 01:16:49.380
than some of his other ones.

1860
01:16:49.380 --> 01:16:53.780
Travel experiences that obviously underscore, you know,

1861
01:16:53.780 --> 01:16:56.990
why those television shows that he did,

1862
01:16:56.990 --> 01:16:58.930
impacted so many people.

1863
01:16:58.930 --> 01:17:01.550
But, you know, a brooding dark guy

1864
01:17:01.550 --> 01:17:05.300
who was an incredible writer and an incredible friend.

1865
01:17:05.300 --> 01:17:06.980
And thinker.
Thinker.

1866
01:17:06.980 --> 01:17:09.750
The person who would really invest a lot of time

1867
01:17:09.750 --> 01:17:11.920
into his friendships and really was curious

1868
01:17:11.920 --> 01:17:13.970
about what made other people tick

1869
01:17:13.970 --> 01:17:18.970
and really appreciated his friends, I think,

1870
01:17:20.220 --> 01:17:22.520
in a way that we can all learn from.

1871
01:17:22.520 --> 01:17:25.720
But I think ultimately where it all really begins to unravel

1872
01:17:25.720 --> 01:17:28.210
is when he gets involved with Asia Argento

1873
01:17:28.210 --> 01:17:30.770
near the end, and she becomes his obsession

1874
01:17:30.770 --> 01:17:34.230
and he remarks early in that relationship,

1875
01:17:34.230 --> 01:17:38.230
a self-awareness that this potentially could be his demise

1876
01:17:38.230 --> 01:17:39.950
and the documentary, I won't spoil it,

1877
01:17:39.950 --> 01:17:41.320
