1884
01:17:57.380 --> 01:18:00.020
I mean, I look at it, as I always say, through the lens

1885
01:18:00.020 --> 01:18:02.150
of recovery and addiction.

1886
01:18:02.150 --> 01:18:05.200
And I just see somebody who is an untreated addict

1887
01:18:05.200 --> 01:18:08.437
and had a profound, you know,

1888
01:18:12.660 --> 01:18:16.800
whether it's a hole in your spirit or an inability

1889
01:18:16.800 --> 01:18:19.730
to just sit with yourself that drove a lot of those

1890
01:18:19.730 --> 01:18:23.160
wild experiences and, you know, compelled him

1891
01:18:23.160 --> 01:18:25.200
to go to places other people wouldn't go,

1892
01:18:25.200 --> 01:18:28.040
you know, like Beirut when it's, you know,

1893
01:18:28.040 --> 01:18:30.290
being bombed and places like that.

1894
01:18:30.290 --> 01:18:32.680
That's part of like, that's a very addict thing.

1895
01:18:32.680 --> 01:18:34.200
Like I need to be where the action is.

1896
01:18:34.200 --> 01:18:37.657
I need to get with the most dramatic woman, you know.

1897
01:18:37.657 --> 01:18:40.500
I need to be where the action is happening

1898
01:18:40.500 --> 01:18:42.880
and that's exciting and it's intoxicating

1899
01:18:42.880 --> 01:18:44.530
and it's ultimately a distraction

1900
01:18:44.530 --> 01:18:48.710
