But I can't even describe this show because,

2244
01:33:31.819 --> 01:33:34.230
like in Bo Burnham's inside,

2245
01:33:34.230 --> 01:33:37.160
it doesn't match up to anything that we're familiar with.

2246
01:33:37.160 --> 01:33:42.160
But Bo's show is even more accessible in a way.

2247
01:33:42.383 --> 01:33:44.592
It's a little more straightforward.

2248
01:33:44.592 --> 01:33:48.350
It's not like, you go from one guest to the next.

2249
01:33:48.350 --> 01:33:51.160
Imagine David Choe covered in head to toe in paint

2250
01:33:51.160 --> 01:33:52.700
and throwing paint on the wall

2251
01:33:52.700 --> 01:33:54.780
and covering his face in clay.

2252
01:33:54.780 --> 01:33:58.180
And then extrapolate that into this show,

2253
01:33:58.180 --> 01:34:02.460
that's a pastiche of interview meets art project

2254
01:34:02.460 --> 01:34:04.700
meets performance art with animations

2255
01:34:04.700 --> 01:34:06.720
and archival footage of him as a kid.

2256
01:34:06.720 --> 01:34:08.640
And great use of extras, dancers.

2257
01:34:08.640 --> 01:34:09.473
Unbelievable.

2258
01:34:09.473 --> 01:34:10.306
Yeah.

2259
01:34:10.306 --> 01:34:12.810
But truly what it is,

2260
01:34:12.810 --> 01:34:17.810
is an excavation of his psyche and a process for him

2261
01:34:18.930 --> 01:34:23.130
to heal his emotional childhood trauma,

2262
01:34:23.130 --> 01:34:25.180
which I think is part and parcel

2263
01:34:25.180 --> 01:34:27.040
of why he lives in his childhood house.

2264
01:34:27.040 --> 01:34:31.083
Like he's a prisoner of certain loops

2265
01:34:31.083 --> 01:34:34.060
that play out in his head that become manifest

2266
01:34:34.060 --> 01:34:37.290
and you can see him struggling with how to overcome them.

2267
01:34:37.290 --> 01:34:40.720
And so many of his conversations are about, you know,

2268
01:34:40.720 --> 01:34:44.570
processing that in real time in conversation with people

2269
01:34:44.570 --> 01:34:48.390
who have analogous childhood trauma experiences.

2270
01:34:48.390 --> 01:34:49.986
And his childhood trauma,

2271
01:34:49.986 --> 01:34:53.660
well, he has two that he talked about in episode two.

2272
01:34:53.660 --> 01:34:56.510
That was, one, is when he was four years old,

2273
01:34:56.510 --> 01:34:58.790
he was sent away to Korea.
Right.

2274
01:34:58.790 --> 01:35:00.640
Ripped away, kike his parents shipped him off

2275
01:35:00.640 --> 01:35:02.250
because they needed to get rid of one kid

2276
01:35:02.250 --> 01:35:05.120
because they had a financial problem, I think

2277
01:35:05.120 --> 01:35:07.840
and they had to like move in with a family members,

2278
01:35:07.840 --> 01:35:09.200
but they didn't want three kids.

2279
01:35:09.200 --> 01:35:12.350
And so they chose him because I think he thought

2280
01:35:12.350 --> 01:35:14.990
he was the odd ball and that just messed with them.

2281
01:35:14.990 --> 01:35:17.260
Imagine being four years old and being sent away,

2282
01:35:17.260 --> 01:35:19.210
it's like, I can't even imagine that.

2283
01:35:19.210 --> 01:35:20.580
And then while he was over there,

2284
01:35:20.580 --> 01:35:22.860
he suspects, he doesn't have clear memories of it,

2285
01:35:22.860 --> 01:35:26.133
but suspects sexual abuse in Korea, I believe so.

2286
01:35:27.910 --> 01:35:30.630
Where I live now is where my childhood trauma happens.

2287
01:35:30.630 --> 01:35:33.670
So that's what I mean by permission,

2288
01:35:33.670 --> 01:35:36.080
it's like a deeper recognition.

2289
01:35:36.080 --> 01:35:37.480
Also an opportunity.

2290
01:35:37.480 --> 01:35:39.533
Like there's a reason why you're back in this house.

2291
01:35:39.533 --> 01:35:44.010
You have an opportunity to not just revisit that past,

2292
01:35:44.010 --> 01:35:46.670
but work through it so that you can develop a new

2293
01:35:46.670 --> 01:35:48.780
and healthier relationship with your past

2294
01:35:48.780 --> 01:35:50.223
and with this domicile.

2295
01:35:51.060 --> 01:35:52.870
I think it's a gift in certain ways

2296
01:35:52.870 --> 01:35:55.150
that might feel uncomfortable right now.

2297
01:35:55.150 --> 01:35:58.070
But I think the show shows you a guy struggling

2298
01:35:58.070 --> 01:36:00.380
in real time with just how to do that.

2299
01:36:00.380 --> 01:36:01.883
It's amazing.

2300
01:36:01.883 --> 01:36:04.870
It's amazing that that's like the key,

2301
01:36:04.870 --> 01:36:06.153
I just didn't expect.

2302
01:36:08.170 --> 01:36:09.101
You gotta make it your own though.

2303
01:36:09.101 --> 01:36:10.680
You gotta work.

2304
01:36:10.680 --> 01:36:12.000
You gotta do the day-to-day stuff.

2305
01:36:12.000 --> 01:36:12.850
And he does do the work.

2306
01:36:12.850 --> 01:36:13.683
He's a deep man.

2307
01:36:13.683 --> 01:36:15.570
He guides them on a guided meditation.

2308
01:36:15.570 --> 01:36:16.960
There's nothing I want more right now

2309
01:36:16.960 --> 01:36:18.371
than the David Choe guided meditation.

2310
01:36:18.371 --> 01:36:20.538
(laughs)

2311
01:36:24.550 --> 01:36:26.030
I think what draws me to him

2312
01:36:26.030 --> 01:36:30.680
is that, it's one thing to say he's he's vulnerable,

2313
01:36:30.680 --> 01:36:33.810
but he has such a big heart.

2314
01:36:33.810 --> 01:36:37.480
Like he leads with his heart, it's right on the surface.

2315
01:36:37.480 --> 01:36:39.230
Like he wants to connect with other people

2316
01:36:39.230 --> 01:36:41.970
so profoundly and you can see his struggle

2317
01:36:41.970 --> 01:36:46.020
